Test Case 2:
Analyze the SWR for a fixed load impedance (ZL) of 50 ohms while varying the characteristic impedance (Zo) of the transmission line to 250 ohms to 400 ohms. Verify how the SWR changes with each value Zo including Zo=ZL.
AIM: To analyze the SWR for a fixed load impedance (ZL) of 75 ohms while varying the characteristic impedance (Zo) of the transmission line to 25 ohms, 50 ohms, 75 ohms, and 100 ohms. To Verify how the SWR changes with each value Zo including Zo=ZL

CODE:
clc;
clear;
close;
ZL = 50;
printf("Zo (Ohms)\tSWR\n");
printf("-------------------------\n");
// When Zo = ZL
Zo = 50;
K = (ZL-Zo)/(ZL+Zo);
S = (1+abs(K))/(1-abs(K));
printf("%d\t\t%f\n", Zo, S);
// Vary Zo from 250 to 400
for Zo = 250:50:400
K = (ZL-Zo)/(ZL+Zo);
S = (1+abs(K))/(1-abs(K));
printf("%d\t\t%f\n", Zo, S);
end

